.TH BYTE_CASE_EQUAL 3 "2023-04-01" "1.0" "lib/byte/byte_case_equal"
.SH NAME
byte_case_equal \- Compare two strings case-insensitively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/byte.h>

.IB size_t
.IB byte_case_equal(const void *s, size_t len, const void *t);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBbyte_case_equal\fR function compares two strings \fIs\fR and \fIt\fR of length \fIl\fR in a case-insensitive manner. It returns 1 if the first \fIl\fR bytes of \fIs\fR are equal to the first \fIl\fR bytes of \fIt\fR, and 0 otherwise.

This function is useful for comparing strings without considering their case.
.SH ARGUMENTS
\fIs\fR
The first string to compare.
\fIl\fR
The length of the strings.
\fIt\fR
The second string to compare.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 if the first \fIl\fR bytes of \fIs\fR are equal to the first \fIl\fR bytes of \fIt\fR, 0 otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBbyte_case_equal\fR function:
.nf
#include <lib/byte.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    const char *str1 = "Hello";
    const char *str2 = "hello";

    if (byte_case_equal(str1, 5, str2)) {
        printf("Strings match case-insensitively\n");
    } else {
        printf("Strings differ case-insensitively\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
.ne
.fi
